Screen Pet brings a small, interactive animal companion to your browser. Choose a pet, give it a name, and enjoy a little company while you work, study, or browse.

NEW: A Harp Seal, birthday celebrations, and daily tarot!

SIX LITTLE FRIENDS
Meet the new Harp Seal alongside the Ginger Cat, brown dog, white dog, Hamster, and Dino. Switch between soft illustrations and pixel art. Your pet, bed, birthday decorations, and tarot cards match the style you choose.

A BIRTHDAY OF THEIR OWN
Your pet's birthday starts with the app installation date, and you can change it in settings. On its birthday, your pet wears a party hat all day. Tap an awake pet to bring out a cake and enjoy a 3-second candle-blowing animation. If your pet is asleep, the first tap wakes it up; tap again to celebrate. Pixel pets get a pixel cake, too.

YOUR DAILY TAROT MOMENT
When your pet is visible between 6 AM and noon, it can offer three face-down cards once that morning. Pick one to reveal a card from the 22 Major Arcana, today's score, a lucky item, and a short reading.

Cards can be upright or reversed, with a different reading and lucky item for each direction. Your first result stays the same for the day across tabs and browser restarts. Missed the morning offer? Right-click your pet and choose Today's Fortune to draw or revisit your card.

Tarot is for fun and reflection, not a prediction of what will happen.

ENGLISH OR KOREAN
Pet dialogue and tarot readings follow your browser language by default: Korean for Korean browsers, English for all other languages. You can also choose English or Korean in settings.

SMALL WAYS TO PLAY
- Drag your pet and set it down anywhere on the page.
- Click for a reaction, or double-click for a little dance.
- Open the right-click menu to feed your pet or start a game.
- Let your cat chase a jingle toy, or play fetch with the other pets.
- Feeding makes your pet rounder; play helps it work that off.
- Tap the bed to send your pet for a nap.

MAKE IT YOURS
Give your pet a name and choose a Cushion, Cat Tower, or Basket. Move its bed along the bottom of the page. Pet choices and settings sync across your open tabs.

NEED A QUIET MOMENT?
Right-click and hide your pet for 10 minutes, 30 minutes, 1 hour, or 1 day. It returns when the timer ends. Your pet appears in the active browser tab, keeping multiple windows from filling up with duplicate companions.

A small friend, a birthday wish, and a daily card — all in your browser.
